Health Analysis Criteria
Green (Sprint Going Well)
Conditions:
- Completion rate > 70%
- Blocked < 2 tasks
- No task >5 days in Progress
- Equitable distribution across team

Message template:

"Sprint {{SPRINT}} is on track. {{DONE_COUNT}}/{{TOTAL_COUNT}} tasks 
completed ({{COMPLETION_RATE}}%). No critical blockers identified. 
Team {{TEAM}} maintains consistent pace. Continue current trajectory."
Yellow (Sprint At Risk)
Conditions:
- 40% < Completion rate < 70%
- 2-3 blocked tasks
- Some tasks in Progress for >5 days
- Workload imbalance on team

Message template:

"Sprint {{SPRINT}} at risk. Only {{COMPLETION_RATE}}% completed with 
{{BLOCKED_COUNT}} blocked tasks. {{SLOW_TASKS}} overdue tasks in 
Progress. {{PERSON}} carries {{OVERLOAD_PCT}}% of work while others have less. 
Action needed in next 2 days."
Red (Sprint Blocked)
Conditions:
- Completion rate < 40%
- > 3 blocked tasks
- Many stalled tasks in Progress
- Or severe bottlenecks

Message template:

"Sprint {{SPRINT}} blocked. Only {{COMPLETION_RATE}}% completion. 
{{BLOCKED_COUNT}} blocked tasks impacting {{IMPACTED_TEAM}}. {{CRITICAL}} 
critical blocker(s) need immediate resolution. Recommendation: stop and unblock today."
Completed (Sprint Done)
Conditions:
- Completion rate = 100% or >95%
- No blockers

Message template:

"Sprint {{SPRINT}} completed successfully. {{TOTAL_COUNT}} tasks done. 
Team {{TEAM}} delivered {{ACHIEVEMENTS}}. Quality: {{QA_STATUS}}."
Action Recommendation

Based on analysis, suggest one concrete action:

If Green:

"Maintain pace. Next sprint can be more aggressive."
"Team in sync. Consider increasing task complexity."

If Yellow:

"Identify top 2 blockers tomorrow and resolve."
"Rebalance workload from {{PERSON}} to {{OTHER_PERSON}}."
"{{BLOCKED_TASKS}} need urgent unblocking. Who can help?"

If Red:

"⚠️ URGENT: Unblocking meeting today with {{STAKEHOLDERS}}."
"Sprint may not close. Consider moving {{TASK_COUNT}} tasks to next sprint."
"Bottleneck at {{BLOCKER}}: allocate {{RESOURCE}} to resolve."

If Completed:

"Excellent work. Retrospective recommended to capture what went well."
